# The per-working-directory run lock (`aether headless` holds an OS advisory
# lock on it while a run is in progress). It is runtime state, not source: the
# file is left behind on disk after every run, so tracking it would make every
# checkout carry a stale artefact.
**/.aether/run.lock
plans/
sweep.timestamp
.astro/
packages/website/dist/
packages/website/.astro/
packages/website/*.log
.DS_Store
# Runtime state under .prairie/ that the runner creates at run-time and
# must NEVER land in the repo (PRAIRIE_* files, per-run logs, deploy state,
# injected-skill state, conflict markers). The deploy recipe files
# (.prairie/deploy.sh, deploy.toml, deploy-state.sh, rollback.sh, healthd.py)
# are NOT ignored and are committed normally.
.prairie/todo.json
.prairie/injected-skills
.prairie/done
.prairie/deployed-commit
.prairie/healthd.pid
.prairie/healthd.log
.prairie-conflicts/
.prairie-conflicts-NOTE.md
test-results/
